From d092c30fbd6567ee9c89a56e9783f8d03f95c16e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Max <dev@zetta.app>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:09:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Normalize sysfs battery type line endings before matching

Native power_supply/type contains Battery followed by a newline. The frontend StringUtil::trim removes only spaces and tabs, so V5 still missed rk817-battery despite its type-based discovery. Strip CR/LF explicitly before trimming and matching.

The earlier host fixture used broader trim semantics and masked this failure. New fixtures link the actual production StringUtil and FileSystemUtil with real symlinked files. Preserved V5 fails LF/CRLF cases and passes the no-newline control; the corrected source passes eleven query/GUI cases, 1080 render cases and three theme cases.

An isolated AArch64 incremental build passes with unchanged dependencies and byte-identical retained V3/V4/V5 trees. Physical acceptance is pending.
---
 es-core/src/platform.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/platform.cpp b/es-core/src/platform.cpp
index c59f7de..24111db 100644
--- a/es-core/src/platform.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/platform.cpp
@@ -295,7 +295,9 @@ std::string queryBatteryRootPath()
 		auto files = Utils::FileSystem::getDirContent("/sys/class/power_supply");
 		for (auto file : files)
 		{
-			auto type = Utils::String::toLower(Utils::String::trim(Utils::FileSystem::readAllText(file + "/type")));
+			auto type = Utils::FileSystem::readAllText(file + "/type");
+			type = Utils::String::toLower(Utils::String::trim(
+				Utils::String::replace(Utils::String::replace(type, "\r", ""), "\n", "")));
 			if (type == "battery" || (type.empty() && Utils::String::toLower(file).find("/bat") != std::string::npos))
 			{
 				batteryRootPath = file;
